# The fly-through's second sample model, a large spider: fourteen parts on spider.vox, z up,
# facing -y; each leg its own part on its own phase. Clips: walk, idle, rear.
#   flythrough --source showcase --model apps/flythrough/assets/entities/spider/spider.rig --clip walk
# Lengths are in model voxels (two to a world voxel at detail 2); `at` is a pivot's rest place
# from its parent's pivot, in the parent's model voxels. The materials are rows of the
# showcase's table with the walker's rows, `_` standing for a space.
vox spider.vox
rate 30
material 1 shell
material 2 rubble
material 3 rock
material 4 ore
material 5 crystal
material 6 amethyst
material 7 ember
material 8 walker
material 9 walker_eye

part body node body at 0 0 25 pivot 11.5 15 3 detail 2
part abdomen node abdomen parent body at 0 13 2 pivot 16.5 1 12 detail 2
part leg_l1 node leg_l1 parent body at -9 -8 0 pivot 60 3 26 detail 2
part leg_r1 node leg_r1 parent body at 9 -8 0 pivot 1 3 26 detail 2
part leg_l2 node leg_l2 parent body at -9 -3 0 pivot 52 3 26 detail 2
part leg_r2 node leg_r2 parent body at 9 -3 0 pivot 1 3 26 detail 2
part leg_l3 node leg_l3 parent body at -9 2 0 pivot 48 3 26 detail 2
part leg_r3 node leg_r3 parent body at 9 2 0 pivot 1 3 26 detail 2
part leg_l4 node leg_l4 parent body at -9 7 0 pivot 58 3 26 detail 2
part leg_r4 node leg_r4 parent body at 9 7 0 pivot 1 3 26 detail 2
part palp_l node palp_l parent body at -4 -14 0 pivot 2 10 7 detail 2
part palp_r node palp_r parent body at 4 -14 0 pivot 2 10 7 detail 2
part fang_l node fang_l parent body at -2 -13 -2 pivot 2 4 8 detail 2
part fang_r node fang_r parent body at 2 -13 -2 pivot 2 4 8 detail 2

